# Migration runner

A schema change exists only as a migration file in the repo, applied by the project's migration runner, so the runner's history table records it. Read the `db-migrations` skill before writing or applying one. That skill names the runner commands.

Urgency does not create an exception. "Just this once", "I'll commit the file later", and "the dashboard is faster" are refusals.

Refuse these, and refuse to recommend them to a human:

- Supabase SQL editor
- Supabase table editor, or any dashboard control that changes schema
- [`psql`](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-psql.html), or any direct session, used to run DDL
- [`supabase db query`](https://supabase.com/docs/reference/cli/supabase-db-query) used to run DDL
- An MCP `execute_sql` call, or an equivalent ad-hoc SQL tool, used to run DDL

Catalog and history inspects may use those tools. DDL may not. If the repo has no runner, stop. Do not invent one, and do not fall back to a dashboard.
